    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d675">

                <pb facs="0800" n="790" xml:id="pg790"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.3516/8–3148: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Dairen</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Paddock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dairen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-31">August 31,
                        1948</date>.<lb/>[Received October 2—11:06 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Rumor discussed locally that Consulate Dairen may close as result closing
                    Vladivostok post. This speculation stems from alleged Nanking Central News
                    broadcasts at 2100 and 2300 hours August 27 reporting Secretary of State news
                    conference that date.</p>
                <p>It appreciated if Embassy verify whether broadcasts mentioned this office.<anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d675-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Dept. Department pass Nanking 38.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paddock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d675-f1" n="6" xml:id="d675-f1-content">
                <p>For reply, see telegram No. 62, October 12, 1 p. m., <ref target="#pg796">p.
